Calibration Workflow	docs/whitepaper/main.tex	/^The projector in our system is mathematically treated as an inverse camera, projecting a 2D digital image onto a physical surface. To map points between the camera's image plane and the projector's output plane on a flat tabletop surface, we utilize homographies. A homography $H$ is a $3 \\times 3$ matrix that relates two planes such that $p_{proj} = H \\cdot p_{cam}$, allowing the system to correctly position digital overlays relative to physical objects viewed by the camera. Furthermore, our system implements parallax correction by intersecting camera rays with a 3D plane at a known height ($z=h$), mapping 2D marker detections back to real-world 3D coordinates.$/;"	s
